            "cABC;circle;circumcircle;A,B,C;0;0;0;0",
            "cFGH;circle;circumcircle;F,G,H;0;0;0;0",
            "pABCDE;polygon;pentagon;A,B,C,D,E;0;0;0;0",
            "pFGHKL;polygon;pentagon;F,G,H,K,L;0;0;0;0",
            // The sides about the equal angles at A and F.
            "AB;line;connect;A,B;0;0;0",
            "AE;line;connect;A,E;0;0;0",
            "FG;line;connect;F,G;0;0;0",
            "FL;line;connect;F,L;0;0;0",
            // The two pairs of equiangular triangles. Explicit ;0 faces.
            "ABE;polygon;triangle;A,B,E;0;0;0;0",
            "FGL;polygon;triangle;F,G,L;0;0;0;0",
            "ABM;polygon;triangle;A,B,M;0;0;0;0",
            "FGN;polygon;triangle;F,G,N;0;0;0;0",
            // "the same circumference": the arcs AB and FG cut off by the
            // angles at E, M and at L, N, each through its midpoint.
            "Wab;point;midpoint;A,B;0;0",
            "Xab;point;cutoff;ABCcenter,Wab,ABCcenter,B;0;0",
            "arcAB;sector;arc;A,Xab,B;0;0;0;0",
            "Wfg;point;midpoint;F,G;0;0",
            "Xfg;point;cutoff;FGHcenter,Wfg,FGHcenter,G;0;0",
            "arcFG;sector;arc;F,Xfg,G;0;0;0;0",
            // Angle markers (see above).
            "angBAE;sector;angleMarker;A,B,E;0;0;3b6ea5;9ec5e8",
            "angGFL;sector;angleMarker;F,G,L;0;0;3b6ea5;9ec5e8",
            "angAEB;sector;angleMarker;E,A,B;0;0;3f8e4f;a8dbb0",
            "angFLG;sector;angleMarker;L,F,G;0;0;3f8e4f;a8dbb0",
            "angAMB;sector;angleMarker;M,A,B;0;0;3f8e4f;a8dbb0",
            "angFNG;sector;angleMarker;N,F,G;0;0;3f8e4f;a8dbb0",
            "rtBAM;sector;angleMarkerRight;A,B,M;0;0;red;red",
            "rtGFN;sector;angleMarkerRight;F,G,N;0;0;red;red",
            "angABM;sector;angleMarker;B,A,M;0;0;c06a1b;f3c590",
            "angFGN;sector;angleMarker;G,F,N;0;0;c06a1b;f3c590"
        ],
        // Draggables (checked against the bundle): A, B, C, F, G free; D, E
        // circleSliders. All are vertices of the given figure and stand from
        // slide 1, so none is deferred. H, K, L (similar), M, N (extend) are
        // derived and listed per slide.
        aliases: { "BA": "AB", "EA": "AE", "GF": "FG", "LF": "FL",
                   "BAE": "angBAE", "EAB": "angBAE",
                   "GFL": "angGFL", "LFG": "angGFL",
                   "AEB": "angAEB", "BEA": "angAEB",
                   "FLG": "angFLG", "GLF": "angFLG",
                   "AMB": "angAMB", "BMA": "angAMB",
                   "FNG": "angFNG", "GNF": "angFNG",
                   "BAM": "rtBAM", "MAB": "rtBAM",
                   "GFN": "rtGFN", "NFG": "rtGFN" },
        slides: [
            { text: "“Similar polygons inscribed in circles are to one another as the squares on their diameters.”",
              visible: DIAM,
              highlighted: ["pABCDE","pFGHKL","BM","GN"],
              justifications: [{ ref: "XII.1" }] },
            { text: "Let {ABC|cABC} and {FGH|cFGH} be circles,",
              visible: GIVEN,
              highlighted: ["cABC","cFGH"] },
            { text: "let {ABCDE|pABCDE} and {FGHKL|pFGHKL} be similar polygons inscribed in them,",
              visible: POLY,
              highlighted: ["pABCDE","pFGHKL"],
              transition: { mode: "parallel", animations: [
                  { elem: "ABCDE", name: geomlib.A.Polygon.outlineAndFill },
                  { elem: "FGHKL", name: geomlib.A.Polygon.outlineAndFill } ] } },
            { text: "and let {BM} and {GN} be diameters of the circles.",
              visible: DIAM,
              highlighted: ["BM","GN"],
              transition: { mode: "parallel", animations: [
                  { elem: "BM", name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeConnect },
                  { elem: "GN", name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeConnect } ] } },
            { text: "I say that the square on {BM} is to the square on {GN}",
              visible: DIAM,
              highlighted: ["BM","GN"] },
            { text: "as the polygon {ABCDE|pABCDE} is to the polygon {FGHKL|pFGHKL}.",
              visible: DIAM,
              highlighted: ["pABCDE","pFGHKL"] },
            { text: "Join {BE}, {AM}, {GL}, and {FN}.",
              visible: JOIN,
              highlighted: ["BE","AM","GL","FN"],
              transition: { mode: "cascade", animations: [
                  { elem: "BE", name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeConnect },
                  { elem: "AM", name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeConnect },
                  { elem: "GL", name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeConnect },
                  { elem: "FN", name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeConnect } ] },
              justifications: [{ ref: "I.Post.1" }] },
            { text: "Now, since the polygon {ABCDE|pABCDE} is similar to the polygon {FGHKL|pFGHKL},",
              visible: SIDES,
              highlighted: ["pABCDE","pFGHKL"] },
            { text: "therefore the angle {BAE} equals the angle {GFL},",
              visible: ANG1,
              highlighted: ["angBAE","angGFL"],
              transition: { mode: "parallel", animations: [
                  { elem: "angBAE", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep },
                  { elem: "angGFL", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep } ] },
              justifications: [{ claim: "similar figures are equiangular", ref: "VI.Def.1" }] },
            { text: "and {BA} is to {AE} as {GF} is to {FL}.",
              visible: ANG1,
              highlighted: ["AB","AE","FG","FL"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "and have the sides about the equal angles proportional", ref: "VI.Def.1" }] },
            { text: "Thus {BAE|ABE} and {GFL|FGL} are two triangles which have one angle equal to one angle,",
              visible: TRI1,
              highlighted: ["ABE","FGL","angBAE","angGFL"] },
            { text: "namely the angle {BAE} equal to the angle {GFL}, and the sides about the equal angles proportional,",
              visible: TRI1,
              highlighted: ["angBAE","angGFL","AB","AE","FG","FL"] },
            { text: "therefore the triangle {ABE} is equiangular with the triangle {FGL}.",
              visible: TRI1,
              highlighted: ["ABE","FGL"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "triangles ABE and FGL equiangular", ref: "VI.6" }] },
            { text: "Therefore the angle {AEB} equals the angle {FLG}.",
              visible: ANG2,
              highlighted: ["angAEB","angFLG"],
              transition: { mode: "parallel", animations: [
                  { elem: "angAEB", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep },
                  { elem: "angFLG", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep } ] } },
            { text: "But the angle {AEB} equals the angle {AMB}, for they stand on {the same circumference|arcAB},",
              visible: ARC,
              highlighted: ["angAEB","angAMB","arcAB"],
              transition: { animations: [
                  { elem: "angAMB", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep } ] },
              justifications: [{ claim: "angles on the same circumference AB", ref: "III.27" }] },
            { text: "and the angle {FLG} equals the angle {FNG},",
              visible: ARC2,
              highlighted: ["angFLG","angFNG","arcFG"],
              transition: { animations: [
                  { elem: "angFNG", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep } ] },
              justifications: [{ claim: "angles on the same circumference FG", ref: "III.27" }] },
            { text: "therefore the angle {AMB} also equals the angle {FNG}.",
              visible: RT.filter(function(n) { return n !== "rtBAM" && n !== "rtGFN"; }),
              highlighted: ["angAMB","angFNG"] },
            { text: "But the right angle {BAM} also equals the right angle {GFN},",
              visible: RT,
              highlighted: ["rtBAM","rtGFN","BM","GN"],
              transition: { mode: "parallel", animations: [
                  { elem: "rtBAM", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep },
                  { elem: "rtGFN", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep } ] },
              justifications: [{ claim: "angles in the semicircles on BM and GN are right", ref: "III.31" }] },
            { text: "therefore {the remaining angle|angABM} equals {the remaining angle|angFGN}.",
              visible: REM,
              highlighted: ["angABM","angFGN"],
              transition: { mode: "parallel", animations: [
                  { elem: "angABM", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep },
                  { elem: "angFGN", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep } ] },
              justifications: [{ claim: "the three angles of a triangle equal two right angles", ref: "I.32" }] },
            { text: "Therefore the triangle {ABM} is equiangular with the triangle {FGN}.",
              visible: TRI2,
              highlighted: ["ABM","FGN"] },
            { text: "Therefore, proportionally {BM} is to {GN} as {BA} is to {GF}.",
              visible: TRI2,
              highlighted: ["BM","GN","AB","FG"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "sides of equiangular triangles ABM, FGN proportional", ref: "VI.4" }] },
            { text: "But the ratio of the square on {BM} to the square on {GN} is duplicate of the ratio of {BM} to {GN},",
              visible: JOIN.concat(["AB","FG"]),
              highlighted: ["BM","GN"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "squares on BM and GN", ref: "VI.20" }] },
            { text: "and the ratio of the polygon {ABCDE|pABCDE} to the polygon {FGHKL|pFGHKL} is duplicate of the ratio of {BA} to {GF}.",
              visible: JOIN.concat(["AB","FG"]),
              highlighted: ["pABCDE","pFGHKL","AB","FG"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "similar polygons ABCDE and FGHKL", ref: "VI.20" }] },
            { text: "Therefore the square on {BM} is to the square on {GN} as the polygon {ABCDE|pABCDE} is to the polygon {FGHKL|pFGHKL}.",
              visible: JOIN,
              highlighted: ["BM","GN","pABCDE","pFGHKL"] },
            { text: "Therefore, similar polygons inscribed in circles are to one another as the squares on their diameters.",
              visible: JOIN,
              highlighted: ["pABCDE","pFGHKL","BM","GN"],
              justifications: [{ ref: "Q.E.D." }] }
        ],
        resolveJustification: function(ref) {
            if (ref === "XII.1") return "#prop";
            return (window.eucrefs && window.eucrefs[ref]) || null;
        }
    });

    // Per-page citation lookup for the slideshow's resolveJustification.
    window.eucrefs = (window.eucrefs || {});
    Object.assign(window.eucrefs, {
        "I.Post.1": "/elements/books/bookI/postulates/post1/",
        "I.32":     "/elements/books/bookI/propositions/propI32/",
        "III.27":   "/elements/books/bookIII/propositions/propIII27/",
        "III.31":   "/elements/books/bookIII/propositions/propIII31/",
        "VI.Def.1": "/elements/books/bookVI/definitions/defVI1/",
        "VI.4":     "/elements/books/bookVI/propositions/propVI4/",
        "VI.6":     "/elements/books/bookVI/propositions/propVI6/",
        "VI.20":    "/elements/books/bookVI/propositions/propVI20/"
    });
</script>
</figure>

Now, since the polygon {ABCDE|pABCDE} is similar to the polygon {FGHKL|pFGHKL}, therefore the angle {BAE} equals the angle {GFL}, and {BA} is to {AE} as {GF} is to {FL}. [!just VI.Def.1]

Thus {BAE|ABE} and {GFL|FGL} are two triangles which have one angle equal to one angle, namely the angle {BAE} equal to the angle {GFL}, and the sides about the equal angles proportional, therefore the triangle {ABE} is equiangular with the triangle {FGL}. Therefore the angle {AEB} equals the angle {FLG}. [!just VI.6]

But the angle {AEB} equals the angle {AMB}, for they stand on the same circumference, and the angle {FLG} equals the angle {FNG}, therefore the angle {AMB} also equals the angle {FNG}. [!just III.27]

But the right angle {BAM} also equals the right angle {GFN}, therefore the remaining angle equals the remaining angle. Therefore the triangle {ABM} is equiangular with the triangle {FGN}. [!just III.31; I.32]

Therefore, proportionally {BM} is to {GN} as {BA} is to {GF}. [!just VI.4]

But the ratio of the square on {BM} to the square on {GN} is duplicate of the ratio of {BM} to {GN}, and the ratio of the polygon {ABCDE|pABCDE} to the polygon {FGHKL|pFGHKL} is duplicate of the ratio of {BA} to {GF}. [!just VI.20]

Therefore the square on {BM} is to the square on {GN} as the polygon {ABCDE|pABCDE} is to the polygon {FGHKL|pFGHKL}.

Therefore, *similar polygons inscribed in circles are to one another as the squares on their diameters.*

<div class="qed">Q.E.D.</div>
<br clear="all">
----
guide:

Proposition @VI.20 states that the ratio of similar polygons is duplicate the ratio of their corresponding sides, so all that is needed is that the corresponding sides are proportional to the diameters of the circumscribed circles, a result that constitutes the bulk of the straightforward proof.

This proposition is in preparation for the next in which it is shown that circles are proportional to the squares on their diameters. The connection is that the circles can be arbitrarily closely approximated by polygons, so that if the polygons are proportional to the squares, then so will the circles be proportional to the squares. The difficulty in that proof coming up is to make that argument rigorous.
